# broiler-tzdb data pin 1
#
# The IANA Time Zone Database release the JavaScript profile's time zone data is generated from.
# Phase F8 (Temporal) opens with it: the repository owner chose on 2026-10-05 to start F8 by
# archiving and pinning tzdb, which answers JSD-0027's owner decision (d) - whether IANA tzdb is
# ever in scope - and JSD-0053 records the boundary. Rule N29 holds the archive to this file.
#
# WHAT IS HERE. The release's data tarball as IANA publishes it, one file, unmodified. A reader
# checks `archive-sha256` without a network. The `member` lines name the files inside it that a
# generator may read, each with its length and SHA-256 after extraction: the nine source files zic
# compiles by default (no `backzone`), `zone.tab` for each country's zones, the `version` file, which
# states the release, and `LICENSE`, which puts the data in the public domain.
#
# HOW IT WAS TAKEN. Retrieved twice on 2026-10-05 from `https://data.iana.org/time-zones/releases/`,
# into two files; `cmp` found them byte-identical, and the first is archived. `archive-sha512` is
# the same file's SHA-512 in the base64 form the npm pins use. IANA also publishes a detached PGP
# signature, `tzdata2026e.tar.gz.asc`; it was not checked, because no key this repository trusts
# signs it, and it is not archived.

data iana-time-zone-database
version 2026e
upstream https://data.iana.org/time-zones/releases/tzdata2026e.tar.gz
retrieved 2026-10-05
retrievals 2 byte-identical
archived yes
